// S441 reproducer — addendum-2 S9g (SECURITY): a `protect=` column returned as a SCALAR (`u.passwordHash`) is
// served to the client at HTTP 200; the egress floor redacts only tagged rows.
// Compiler SHA: cf62b4154 (origin/main at dispatch)
// Command: bun compiler/bin/scrml.js compile docs/changes/s441-audit-gap-filing/repro/site-protected-column-escapes-redaction-as-scalar.scrml --output-dir <scratch>
// Expected: §14.8.9 "Every compiler-emitted client-egress serializer — a server-function response, … — SHALL
//           **strip, by construction, every column whose provenance origin is a `protect=` field**, before the
//           value crosses to the client … The strip keys on the column's resolved source `(table, column)`
//           origin, never its surface name … it is sound *by construction*."
// Actual:   exit 0; the only protect diagnostic is `info [I-PROTECT-STRIP-001]: the egress floor strips protected
//           column(s) `passwordHash` from the client response …` — which is false for this return. server.js:
//           `const u = _scrml_protect_tag((await _scrml_sql`SELECT passwordHash …`)[0] ?? null, ["passwordHash"]);`
//           `return u.passwordHash;` → `JSON.stringify(_scrml_protect_redact(_scrml_result) ?? null)`; the
//           redactor sees a plain string with no origin descriptor. EXECUTED (seeded row passwordHash =
//           'SECRET-HASH-123', authenticated session + synchronizer token, called the emitted route handler):
//           `status 200 body "SECRET-HASH-123"`. Any value derived from the column (a member read, a
//           concatenation, a destructure) leaves the tag behind. Sibling of
//           G-PROTECT-TAG-TOJSON-HOOK-DROPPED-BY-OBJECT-SPREAD (same tag-on-the-row design).
<program db="./fresh-protect.db">
<schema>
  users {
    id: integer primary key
    name: text
    passwordHash: text
  }
</schema>
<db src="./fresh-protect.db" tables="users" protect="passwordHash"/>
function getHash() {
    const u = ?{`SELECT passwordHash FROM users WHERE id = 1`}.get()
    return u.passwordHash
}
<h> = ""
<button onclick=${ @h = getHash() }>x</button>
<p>${@h}</p>
</program>
